  message: "DONE — merged as PR #898, dev b1900202e0. Closed on the FILED ROW under the\n2026-09-10 drain criterion (ruling c): correct, zero losses, rows read back\nagainst source. Record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/kikar_js_09102026/RESULT.md\n\nTHE FILED ROW IS FIXED, AND IT WAS SMALLER THAN THE DEFECT. This item named the\ntwo METHOD-kind rows (process.on for the fork channel, process.send). The break\nwas in the member-call path, not the row kind, so the FUNCTION-kind rows on\n`process` were equally unreachable — hrtime, uptime, getuid, memoryUsage, chdir,\nopenStdin — and `performance.now()` was a SECOND global with the same shape that\nthis item does not mention at all. Enumerating every method/function-kind module\nin javascript.yaml against its resolution route found exactly two modules with no\nroute: process and performance. The item's own hint (\"check the other node\nglobals rowed as methods: Deno\") was answered — Deno was already admitted — but\nthe enumeration was what found performance.\n\nMEASURED, vscode / nextjs / podman-desktop, one arm per committed blob, blob\nasserted before each arm, identity keyed on (src, line, callee) rather than on\nthe `dst` the change modifies:\n\n    repo             calls OFF   calls ON   moved\n    vscode              10,459     10,459      41\n    nextjs             285,110    285,110     832\n    podman-desktop         502        502      19\n\n**calls_total IDENTICAL in all three — re-labels, mints nothing.**\n**892 promotions and EVERY ONE came off `external`. ZERO thefts.**\n    external -> process     450\n    external -> performance 442\nThat zero is the number that mattered: Case 3b fires only where nothing else\nresolved, so a promotion off an already-RESOLVED symbol would be a regression\nwearing a recall figure's clothes (WI-vihop had exactly that, 24 edges bound to\nan interface declaration). Diffing both ways, grouped by the OLD slot, separates\nthem.\n\n892 IS THE PROMOTION COUNT; **278 IS THE RECALL FIGURE** — promotions landing on\nan actual catalogue row (performance.now 212, process.on 23, process.hrtime 20,\nprocess.getuid 10, process.chdir 5, process.send 4, getgid 2, cpuUsage 1,\numask 1). The other 614 are correctly slotted members the catalogue does not row.\nRecorded as two numbers deliberately: quoting 892 as recall would pool a real\ngain with a correct no-op.\n\nTAGGED `awaits_bakeoff_validation`: the counts above are quantitative corpus\nclaims. NOTE WHAT IS **NOT** DONE — this item's own acceptance criterion is the\nTAINT PATH (\"ipc_recv mints untrusted_input and ipc_send is a sink, so both sides\nadd findings; marginal precision on the new findings\"). This measurement prices\nREACHABILITY, not findings. The 27 newly-reached ipc rows (process.on 23,\nprocess.send 4) are where that check would land, and it is owed at validation\ntime rather than claimed here.\n\nRESIDUALS FILED, neither folded in:\n  WI-bomuh — process.cwd is rowed `kind: attribute` though Node's process.cwd()\n    is a FUNCTION, so 135 corpus call sites are now correctly slotted and STILL\n    unmatchable. Not an absent row: a wrong row that looks present. The\n    attribute-vs-callable mis-kind is probably not unique to it.\n  WI-nukub — JS_KNOWN_GLOBALS claimed to \"mirror javascript.yaml\" and did not.\n    It cannot be DERIVED the way the adjacent _derive_js_constructor_types is,\n    because the catalogue records no field saying how a module is REACHED\n    (global / import / constructor). A third global rowed tomorrow fails\n    silently exactly as these two did. The false claim is removed and the real\n    constraint stated; the derivation needs a schema field."  # c645
